[[:db/retract 17592186120247 :question/answer-fields 17592186117641] {:db/id 17592186119829 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fae89980-f6bf-5229-9ea3-54197530dd8b" "question-bced3755-fd06-539b-819f-10c4ab686823"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119831 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8bddb63c-4c54-5e88-a8e9-1298e5060eb6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119642 :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n![](images/89/89e1a065666c566dcd8a7648a0087045eadc0132c1933357f4b60a06103ffa0f.svg)\n\nThe direction vector of the line is $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1\\rangle,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =⟨\\sqrt{2},0,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-fae89980-f6bf-5229-9ea3-54197530dd8b" :question/id #uuid "fae89980-f6bf-5229-9ea3-54197530dd8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127645" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(3,-2,4)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨1,-2,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-2,4⟩,$ and $n=⟨1,-2,-1⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ & =⟨3,-2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5979170b-e938-5576-b257-2c5e77488161"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5979170b-e938-5576-b257-2c5e77488161" :answer-field/id #uuid "5979170b-e938-5576-b257-2c5e77488161" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-afd07518-3061-5b76-96ee-db6a415e76db" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25d0e859-47cf-5e2e-9ce5-c53b1448f6f2" "answer-061185a3-b68f-5683-8fef-601edcc7e95a" "answer-e2856d01-e48b-5c22-b7b4-3fdd89bdafd8" "answer-b94406b8-9d2b-52e2-8a01-3a285d79c857" "answer-afd07518-3061-5b76-96ee-db6a415e76db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25d0e859-47cf-5e2e-9ce5-c53b1448f6f2" :answer/id #uuid "25d0e859-47cf-5e2e-9ce5-c53b1448f6f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,1⟩=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-061185a3-b68f-5683-8fef-601edcc7e95a" :answer/id #uuid "061185a3-b68f-5683-8fef-601edcc7e95a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-1⟩=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2856d01-e48b-5c22-b7b4-3fdd89bdafd8" :answer/id #uuid "e2856d01-e48b-5c22-b7b4-3fdd89bdafd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b94406b8-9d2b-52e2-8a01-3a285d79c857" :answer/id #uuid "b94406b8-9d2b-52e2-8a01-3a285d79c857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afd07518-3061-5b76-96ee-db6a415e76db" :answer/id #uuid "afd07518-3061-5b76-96ee-db6a415e76db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bced3755-fd06-539b-819f-10c4ab686823" :question/id #uuid "bced3755-fd06-539b-819f-10c4ab686823" :question/math-academy-id "q-32972" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(5,-1,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨-1,-2,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨5,-1,1⟩$ and $n=⟨-1,-2,3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩ & =⟨5,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c10fc8bb-0d7f-5bee-84f8-1fa8a92dd2ab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c10fc8bb-0d7f-5bee-84f8-1fa8a92dd2ab" :answer-field/id #uuid "c10fc8bb-0d7f-5bee-84f8-1fa8a92dd2ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-32743a37-ea98-5030-bc97-5c9249817938" :answer-field/choices ["answer-32743a37-ea98-5030-bc97-5c9249817938" "answer-c3bbba03-77ef-54a0-90c6-08b40f6f1852" "answer-a556e4c0-7956-5861-be5e-2d8ead0ef5eb" "answer-6906bd4d-81fa-56e9-9975-333718bd9981" "answer-3bf9d08c-d107-5f44-9c81-8ad84d2c8cae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32743a37-ea98-5030-bc97-5c9249817938" :answer/id #uuid "32743a37-ea98-5030-bc97-5c9249817938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3bbba03-77ef-54a0-90c6-08b40f6f1852" :answer/id #uuid "c3bbba03-77ef-54a0-90c6-08b40f6f1852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a556e4c0-7956-5861-be5e-2d8ead0ef5eb" :answer/id #uuid "a556e4c0-7956-5861-be5e-2d8ead0ef5eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩=⟨-5,1,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6906bd4d-81fa-56e9-9975-333718bd9981" :answer/id #uuid "6906bd4d-81fa-56e9-9975-333718bd9981" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨5,-1,1⟩=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bf9d08c-d107-5f44-9c81-8ad84d2c8cae" :answer/id #uuid "3bf9d08c-d107-5f44-9c81-8ad84d2c8cae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨5,-1,1⟩=⟨1,2,-3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8bddb63c-4c54-5e88-a8e9-1298e5060eb6" :question/id #uuid "8bddb63c-4c54-5e88-a8e9-1298e5060eb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-70883" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(1,3,5).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(1,3,5)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,3,5⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,2,5⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩ & =⟨1,2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩ & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-09321377-3d24-5a5f-8608-652765793fba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-09321377-3d24-5a5f-8608-652765793fba" :answer-field/id #uuid "09321377-3d24-5a5f-8608-652765793fba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c846c53c-a7c1-5cb9-84b1-15cf24c5ceca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5c482fb6-1221-56a1-9d24-627eff7b967c" "answer-c846c53c-a7c1-